      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p37_b5",
      "text": "RLHF; Rafailov et al. [2024] show that the same phenomenon persists in direct alignment\nalgorithms; and Hosking et al. [2024] argue that human-feedback scores themselves\ncan be misaligned with true quality because they over-reward stylistic features such as\nassertiveness. On the mitigation side, one family of papers tries to improve the reward\n",
      "bbox": [
