      "block_id": "2605.00155_p37_b13",
      "text": "Zhai et al. [2024] penalize reward uncertainty estimated from LoRA ensembles, Xu et al.\n[2025] learn a pessimistic reward model, and Yan et al. [2024] optimize a reward-robust\npolicy objective. A third family regularizes the policy toward regions where the reward\nmodel is thought to be reliable. Moskovitz et al. [2024] impose explicit constraints in\nRLHF, Dai et al. [2025] regularize toward behavior-supported regions, Rita et al. [2024]\nuse demonstration-guided reinforcement learning, and Liu et al. [2024] show that SFT\nloss can play the role of an adversarial regularizer. These methods are important points\nof comparison for us because they reveal the central tension: protecting against reward\n",
      "bbox": [
